      {
        "id": 51934,
        "name": "Victor Mancha",
        "username": "Victor_Mancha",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/v/ed8c4c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-01-16T10:59:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hi guys,</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>new session, new questions ^_^u</p><p>So, I played a new solo game yesterday: Haka, Bunker and Absolute Zero (plus Fanatic incapacitated from the start) versus Omnitron in the ruins of Atlantis. Man, that was an embarrassing defeat if I ever saw one. I only got to deal 49 damage to Omnitron before two of those pesky Krakens killed my last two heroes in play.&nbsp;</p><p>Anyways, let's not dwell on that xD</p><p>My question are:</p><p><strong>Toxic Seaweed: </strong>At the end of the enviroment turn one player may discard their hand to destroy this card.&nbsp;</p><p>So, if a player has no cards on their hand, can they decide to discard their zero cards hand and destroy the card? I assume so, but I'd like confirmation.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And the other question. One of the powers of Fanatic when incapacitated reads:&nbsp;</p><p>Select a heroes. Increase the next damage dealt by that hero by 2.</p><p>So I have Bunker, and he plays <strong>External Combustion</strong>: Bunker deals himself 2 fire damage and deals each non-hero target 3 fire damage.</p><p>My question is:</p><p>Does he deals himself 4 fire damage and each non-hero target 5 fire damage?</p><p>Does he deals himself 4 fire damage and each non-hero targets 3 fire damage?</p><p>Can he deal himself 2 fire damage, one of the non-hero targets 5 fire damage, and 3 fire damge to the rest of non-hero targets?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thanlks in advance, guys. This game rules but it gives me a bit of a headache on occasions :P</p>",
        "post_number": 28,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:25:41.829Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
