        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/{size}/1925_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-01-16T11:16:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yes, as toxic seaweed is discard a hand rather than number of cards, you an dsicard an empty 'hand' to get rid of it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And the second interpretation is correct. It literally means the next damage dealt. It is like Haka of Battle and Taiha, or Rampage. Only the first hit gets the boost.</p>",
