        "created_at": "2013-01-20T01:38:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Victor Mancha\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Victor Mancha:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;One of the powers of Fanatic when incapacitated reads:&nbsp;Select a heroes. Increase the next damage dealt by that hero by 2.So I have Bunker, and he plays <strong>External Combustion</strong>:Bunker deals himself 2 fire damage and deals each non-hero target 3 fire damage.My question is:Does he deals himself 4 fire damage and each non-hero target 5 fire damage?Does he deals himself 4 fire damage and each non-hero targets 3 fire damage?Can he deal himself 2 fire damage, one of the non-hero targets 5 fire damage, and 3 fire damge to the rest of non-hero targets?&nbsp;Thanlks in advance, guys. This game rules but it gives me a bit of a headache on occasions <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/stuck_out_tongue.png?v=12\" title=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The middle one. he deals himself 4 fire damage and each non-hero target 3. the \"next damage\" in the ability refers to the next damage dealt. this is the same idf bunker played a card that dealt damaged thehn used a power that dealt more damage</p>",
